    <!-- How to play / leaving -->
    <string name="backgammon_help_title">How to Play Backgammon</string>
    <string name="backgammon_help_body">Race all 15 of your checkers around the board and off it before your opponent does.\n\nEach turn you roll two dice and move checkers by those numbers, one die at a time. A double gives you four moves. Tap one of your highlighted checkers, then a highlighted destination.\n\nA point with two or more enemy checkers is blocked. A lone enemy checker (a blot) is hit and sent to the bar, and a checker on the bar must enter before you can move anything else. You must play both dice if you can, otherwise the larger one if only one can be played.\n\nOnce all 15 of your checkers are in your home board you can bear them off, with the exact number or, if no checker is farther back, a larger one.\n\nA normal win scores 1 point, a gammon (the loser has borne off nothing) 2 points, and a backgammon (a gammon with a loser\'s checker still on the bar or in your home board) 3 points. There is no doubling cube.\n\nAt the start each side rolls one die and the higher roll goes first, using both numbers.</string>
    <string name="backgammon_leave_title">Leave this game?</string>
    <string name="backgammon_leave_body">This game is still in progress. Leaving now won\'t count it as a win or a loss.</string>
    <string name="backgammon_leave_body_session">This game is still in progress and won\'t count, but the games you\'ve already finished stay on your record.</string>

